Chapter: RealModeOpening

 An `opening` that RETURNS a moded Real, which is a different walk from
 `show` and was broken for as long as the modes existed.

 `emit-opening-result-print` matched `RealTy` alone and its tail is
 `otherwise -> st`, which emits nothing at all. So a program whose entry
 point returned `Real trapping` printed NO OUTPUT -- not a wrong number, no
 line. `real-mode-show` cannot see it: that test calls `show` inside an act
 block, which is `emit-show-builtin`, a walk that asks `is-real-type` and
 was always right.

 The distinction matters for the pin: a test that prints a moded Real is
 not a test that RETURNS one, and only the second reaches this emitter.

Section: Entry

  opening : Real trapping
  opening = to-real-trapping 2.5
